//!
//! # Time
//!
//! The kernel's clock: the periodic timer tick, the uptime derived from it and
//! the calibration of the local APIC timer against the PIT.
//!
//! ## Public API
//!
//! | Name          | File        | Purpose                                                                     |
//! |---------------|-------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Time::Timer` | `timer.ign` | `initialize` (calibrate and start), `report`, `ticks`, `uptimeMilliseconds` |
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! | Imports   | Why                                                      |
//! |-----------|----------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Arch`    | the PIT is the reference clock, `Cpu` enables interrupts |
//! | `Apic`    | the local APIC timer is the tick source                  |
//! | `Drivers` | `Timer::report` prints the calibration                   |
//!
//! `Sched` imports `Time` to sleep for a number of ticks, and `Trap` calls
//! `Time::Timer::handleTick` from the timer interrupt.

import _ from "./timer";

/// Aggregate namespace of the clock. The file above contributes
/// `Time::Timer`.
export namespace Time {}
